'''telary''' (tel′a-ri), ''a.'' [< ML. *''telarius'', < L. ''tela'', a web: see ''tela.''] '''1.''' Of or pertaining to a web, tissue, or tela; woven; spun.—'''2†.''' Spinning a web, as a spider; telarian.
